:: Basement - slave party introduction [bg-basement]
<h1 class="ptitle">BASEMENT</h1>
<br />

<<set _mistressIds = setup.getPersonsForLocation($guests, 'mistress')>>
<<set _introPresenter = _mistressIds.length ? $guests[_mistressIds[0]] : null>>
<<set _introIsAttendant = false>>
<<if !_introPresenter>>
    <<set _attGuestQual = setup.getPersonsForLocation($guests, 'attendant').find(id => $guests[id].relationship > 60)>>
    <<set _attSlaveQual = setup.getPersonsForLocation($slaves, 'attendant').find(id => $slaves[id].relationship > 60)>>
    <<if typeof _attGuestQual !== 'undefined'>>
        <<set _introPresenter = $guests[_attGuestQual]>>
        <<set _introIsAttendant = true>>
    <<elseif typeof _attSlaveQual !== 'undefined'>>
        <<set _introPresenter = $slaves[_attSlaveQual]>>
        <<set _introIsAttendant = true>>
    <</if>>
<</if>>

<<set _slaves = setup.getAvailablePersons18yo($slaves)>>
<<set _randomSlave = $slaves[setup.getRandomElement(_slaves[0] ?? _slaves[1])]>>
<<set _npc = _randomSlave>>
<<set _npc.location = 'basement'>>

<<set _url = _npc.gender == 1 ? 'male' : 'female'>>
<center>
    [img[setup.ImagePath+'places/basement/mistress_' + _url + '.jpg']]
</center>
<br />
<<if _introIsAttendant>>
    As you stepped into the basement, <<=setup.displayName(_introPresenter)>> paused mid-task, hands still damp, and turned to face you with a thoughtful look.
    <br /><br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        I've been thinking... these people work hard. A proper gathering — food, something to drink — it might do them a world of good.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    You raised an eyebrow, curious where this was going.
    <br /><br />
    <<you>>
        Go on.
    <</you>>
    <br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        Clean bodies, full bellies, a little music. They'd feel human again for a night. Happier people cause less trouble, and they work better for it.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    It was a practical argument, delivered with quiet sincerity.
    <br /><br />
    <<you>>
        And what would you need?
    <</you>>
    <br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        Food enough for everyone, and something to celebrate with. Leave the rest to me.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    <br />
<<else>>
    As you descended into the dank basement, the <<=setup.displayName(_introPresenter)>>'s chilling presence hung heavy in the air, casting long shadows across the stone walls.
    <<=setup.pronounceWho(_introPresenter, true)>> piercing gaze met yours as you approached.
    <br /><br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        I have an idea. A way to tighten our grip on these wretched souls.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    You braced yourself for what was to come, knowing all too well the depths of her depravity.
    <br /><br />
    <<you>>
        Go on
    <</you>>
    <br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        We shall host a feast. A celebration of their submission, a testament to our absolute control.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    Your stomach churned at the thought, but you dared not show weakness in the presence of such malevolence.
    <br /><br />
    <<you>>
        And what purpose will this serve?
    <</you>>
    <br />
    <<=setup.pronounceWho(_introPresenter, true)>> laughter echoed off the walls, a discordant symphony of madness and malice.
    <br /><br />
    <<sayNpc _introPresenter>>
        To break them or to make them more happy?... Your choice.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    You swallowed hard, the bitter taste of fear coating your tongue like poison.
    <br /><br />
<</if>>
<<if _npc>>
    <center>
        <<actionImage _npc begging>>
    </center>
    <br />
    <<sayNpc _npc>>
        Please sir! We would do anything for a decent meal and something outside these cages.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
<</if>>
<<linkreplace 'Leave'>>
    <<if _introIsAttendant>>
        You gave a slow nod. <<=setup.displayName(_introPresenter)>> smiled — the quiet, satisfied kind — and got back to work, already planning.
    <<else>>
        As you turned to leave, the Mistress's laughter followed you like a ghostly specter, a haunting reminder of the darkness that dwelled within us all.
        And in the depths of that desolate basement, where shadows danced with the echoes of suffering, you knew that the true horrors had only just begun.
    <</if>>
    <<set $player.quests.slave_party = true>>
    <<set $locationEvents.basement = true>>
    <br /><br />
    <strong>Now you can throw parties for slaves.</strong>
    <br /><br />
    <<link 'Leave'>>
        <<goto 'Basement'>>
    <</link>>
<</linkreplace>>
